# =============================================================================
# ADR-12 SCAN FACE 3  --  DERIVED FIELDS AND DERIVED VERDICT WORDING
# =============================================================================
# Authority : ADR-12 (arch-decisions-lead-2026-09-19.md section 12)
#             architecture-saas-2026-09-19.md section 12 扫描面表
#               (X-2 build-time ; 扫描面 3 · 派生字段)
#             contract-t6-api-freeze-2026-09-19.md
#               - section 2.8 domain H 措辞纪律自查 (client-visible fields must
#                 pass section 5.1 R1~R8)
#               - section 4.4 三类失败在契约中的区分与表达
#               - the client-visible error-code table
#             integration-metric-spec-2026-09-16.md sections 3.2 / 4.3
# Owner     : see ../owners.csv  ->  subject = scan3_derived
# Encoding  : UTF-8 (readers MUST decode as UTF-8, never as platform ANSI/GBK)
#
# CITATION RULE: semantic anchors only (section / rule id / item title / config
# number / function name), never line numbers -- see wordlists/scan1_refund.words.
#
# Rationale: derived fields and derived verdicts are computed server-side and
# are NOT downloadable to the client. The internal gap-reason enum and the
# client sync-state enum are two independent enum namespaces and MUST NOT share
# a type definition (contract section 4.2 / 4.3, 契约级隔离). A client build that
# merely *names* one of
# these identifiers has already leaked the concept.
#
# FORMAT
#   one term per line; '#' starts a comment.
#   ASCII identifier-like terms are matched with word boundaries and
#   case-insensitively; all other terms are matched as substrings.
# =============================================================================

## group: derived field / identifier names
gap_reason
effect_verdict
AS_refund
a3_value
a3_applicable
is_compliant
achievement_rate
adherence_state
risk_flag
coverage_flag

## group: derived field names that were MISSING until 2026-09-24
#   TRIGGER (S1-6, 2026-09-24)
#     The client package carried the path `/api/v1/band/derived` in its own
#     allow-list -- an endpoint the contract denies to the client (row E4,
#     x-client-explicitly-denied: true). The gate reported PASS.
#     Two independent reasons, and BOTH had to be fixed:
#       (a) the concept word `derived` was simply not a term, so no face could
#           fire on it;
#       (b) several derived FIELD names ruled client-invisible by the contract
#           visibility matrix were also absent from this file.
#
#   WHY THIS IS NOT "JUST ADD THE WORD"
#     Adding `derived` alone would have been a word-scan patch on a defect whose
#     real shape is a DRIFT problem: this wordlist and the contract's visibility
#     matrix are two hand-maintained lists of the same fact, and nothing kept
#     them in step. So the term is added here AND a companion gate
#     (`client-zero-derived-gate.py`, S1-6) now derives the forbidden field-name
#     set mechanically from `contract/visibility/band-visibility-matrix.json`
#     (every field of every group whose `client` value is false), so the next
#     field added to ③/④ is caught even if nobody remembers this file.
#
#   CURATION: all terms here are full field names, never a bare fragment, for
#   the same reason the note below rejects the bare "temp" -- ASCII terms are
#   matched at the SEGMENT level, so a short term fires on innocent identifiers
#   and a gate nobody can explain gets switched off. `adherence_state` stays even
#   though it is a ③-adjacent name, because a client build that merely NAMES it
#   has already leaked the concept.
derived
adherence_dimension_score
a3
refund_eligibility
improvement_rate

